  make:{t:"สร้างระบบหนึ่งชุดที่รันได้จริงทุกสัปดาห์ พร้อมจุดอนุมัติของคนและ log",d:"มันรันเองครบสองสัปดาห์ติดกัน โดยคุณไม่ต้องเข้าไปแตะ"},
  show:{t:"พาเพื่อนร่วมทีมดูทีละขั้น ให้เขาชี้ว่าจุดไหนน่าจะพังก่อน"}},

 {n:"พิสูจน์ชั่วโมงที่ประหยัดได้",gate:false,out:"เอกสารหนึ่งหน้า ส่งถึงหัวหน้า",
  watch:{t:"พิสูจน์ชั่วโมงที่ประหยัดได้",d:"3 นาที 30 วินาที"},
  prompt:"ช่วยเรียบเรียงข้อมูลด้านล่างเป็นเอกสารหนึ่งหน้าสำหรับผู้จัดการ แบ่งเป็นสี่หัวข้อ — งานอะไร เวลาก่อนและหลัง ชั่วโมงต่อปี และความเสี่ยงที่เหลืออยู่พร้อมวิธีคุม ใช้เฉพาะตัวเลขที่ผมให้ ห้ามปัดขึ้น ห้ามเพิ่มคำโฆษณา จบด้วยหนึ่งบรรทัดว่าระบบนี้ยังทำอะไรไม่ได้",
  expect:"หนึ่งหน้าที่หัวหน้าอ่านจบในหนึ่งนาที หัวข้อที่คนลืมคือข้อสี่ — ความเสี่ยงที่เหลือ แต่มันคือหัวข้อที่ทำให้ผู้บริหารเชื่อคุณ",
  stuck:"อย่าปัดตัวเลขขึ้น ถ้าประหยัดได้ 28 นาที ก็เขียน 28 นาที ตัวเลขเล็กที่จริงมีน้ำหนักกว่าตัวเลขใหญ่ที่ตรวจสอบไม่ได้ ถ้าหัวหน้าจับได้ว่าปัดขึ้น เขาจะไม่เชื่อทั้งหน้า",
  calc:true,
  make:{t:"ส่งเอกสารหนึ่งหน้าให้หัวหน้า แล้วขอสองอย่าง — เวลาสำหรับงานถัดไป และเพื่อนร่วมทีมอีกหนึ่งคนมาเรียนด้วย",d:"หัวหน้าได้อ่านจริง และคุณได้คำตอบ ไม่ว่าจะใช่หรือไม่"},
  show:{t:"โพสต์สรุปสั้น ๆ ให้ทีมเห็น พร้อมพรอมป์ที่คุณใช้ ให้คนอื่นเอาไปใช้ต่อได้"}}
],
en:[
 {n:"Find the five tasks you repeat every week",gate:false,out:"A list of five tasks with scores",
  watch:{t:"Find the five tasks you repeat every week",d:"3 min"},
  noai:["For one week, log every time you repeat something — the task and roughly how long it took.",
        "At the end of the week, score two things: hours per month, and how tedious it is, 1–5.",
        "Multiply them. The highest score is your task for the next station.",
        "Rule out: anything involving customer data or pricing, and anything you do once a year."],
  expect:"The list usually looks similar for everyone — the weekly report, answering the same customer email, reformatting an Excel export, writing up meeting notes, chasing another team.",
  stuck:"Most people open an AI tool first and then look for work to feed it. That produces a toy, not your time back. Also: don't pick the hardest task — pick the most repeated one.",
  make:{t:"Write the five tasks with hours × tedium scores, and circle the highest.",d:"You can point to your first task and justify it with numbers."},
  show:{t:"Show the list to a teammate and ask whether their five are the same. If they are, you've found a team problem, not a personal one."}},

 {n:"Rewrite one task, at half the time",gate:false,out:"A reusable prompt + before/after times",
  watch:{t:"Rewrite one task, at half the time",d:"3 min 40 sec"},
  prompt:"You are assisting a warehouse manager. Summarise the data below for the plant manager. Maximum 200 words. Three headings: performance, problems, decisions needed. Use only the figures provided — do not estimate. If data is missing, write 'no data'.",
  expect:"A prompt that works states four things: who you are, who's reading, the output shape, and what it must not do. The line 'if data is missing, write no data' is the critical one — without it, the model fills gaps with figures that look reasonable and aren't real.",
  stuck:"'Summarise this' returns something generic that needs rewriting entirely — no time saved. Also: time yourself before you start. Without a baseline you can't prove anything at Station 4.",
  calc:true,
  make:{t:"Save the working prompt somewhere you'll reach for it weekly, then time the task again.",d:"The task is measurably faster and you've written down both numbers."},
  show:{t:"Send the output to the person who actually reads it, and ask whether the quality held. Faster but worse is not a pass."}},

 {n:"Automate two steps",gate:true,out:"A weekly automation + human approval + log",
  watch:{t:"Automate two steps — and keep a human in the loop",d:"5 min"},
  noai:["The structure has exactly three parts — trigger, AI step, human approval. There is no fourth part.",
        "Example: Monday morning, pull the export, have AI format and summarise it, send the draft to your inbox.",
        "The prompt from Station 2 drops straight into the AI step. That's why Station 2 isn't skippable.",
        "Log every run — when it ran, and on what data."],
  expect:"An automation that sends nothing to anyone on its own. Everything ends as a draft in your inbox. Drag-and-drop tools are fine — no code needed.",
  stuck:"Feed it a file with the columns in the wrong format. It will still produce a summary, with wrong numbers and no warning — the system doesn't know it's wrong. That's why a person reads it first. And this is still your work: 'the AI did it' is not an explanation anyone accepts.",
  make:{t:"Build one automation that runs weekly, with a human approval step and a log.",d:"It has run on its own for two consecutive weeks without you touching it."},
  show:{t:"Walk a teammate through it step by step and have them point at what will break first."}},

 {n:"Prove the hours you saved",gate:false,out:"A one-page document sent to your manager",
  watch:{t:"Prove the hours you saved",d:"3 min 30 sec"},
  prompt:"Turn the data below into a one-page document for a manager. Four sections: what the task is, time before and after, hours per year, and what risk remains with how it's controlled. Use only the figures I give you — do not round up, do not add promotional language. End with one line on what this still can't do.",
  expect:"One page a manager reads in a minute. The section people leave out is the fourth — remaining risk — and it's the one that makes leadership trust you.",
  stuck:"Don't inflate. If you saved 28 minutes, write 28 minutes. A small true number carries more weight than a big unverifiable one — if your manager catches you rounding up, they stop believing the whole page.",
  calc:true,
  make:{t:"Send the one-pager and ask for two things: time for the next task, and one teammate to go through this with you.",d:"Your manager has actually read it, and you have an answer either way."},
  show:{t:"Post a short summary for the team, including the prompt you used, so someone else can pick it up."}}
]};

let lang="th",idx=0,done={},gateOK=[false,false,false],calc={b:"",a:"",f:""};
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),U=()=>UI[lang];

function rail(){
  const T=U();
  $("srail").innerHTML=S[lang].map((s,i)=>{
    const dn=(done[i]||[]).length===4;
    return `<button data-i="${i}" aria-current="${i===idx}">
      <span class="num">${i+1}</span><span class="nm">${s.n}</span>
      ${s.gate?`<span class="st gate">${T.gate}</span>`:dn?`<span class="st done">✓ ${T.doneTag}</span>`:""}
    </button>`}).join("");
  $("srail").querySelectorAll("button").forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{idx=+b.dataset.i;render();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:"smooth"})});
}
function calcOut(){
  const T=U(),b=+calc.b||0,a=+calc.a||0,f=+calc.f||0;
  const perM=Math.max(0,(b-a))*f, perY=(perM*12/60), pct=b>0?Math.round((1-a/b)*100):0;
  return `<div class="cout">
    <div><b>${perM||0}</b><span>${T.cSaveM}</span></div>
    <div><b>${perY?perY.toFixed(1):"0"}</b><span>${T.cSaveY}</span></div>
    <div><b>${pct>0?pct:0}%</b><span>${T.cPct}</span></div></div>
    <p class="cwarn">${T.cWarn}</p>`;
}
function chk(i){
  const on=(done[idx]||[]).includes(i);
  return `<div class="donebox"><button class="check" data-s="${i}" aria-pressed="${on}">✓</button><p><b>${U().markDone}</b></p></div>`;
}
function render(){
  const T=U(),s=S[lang][idx];
  $("brand").textContent=T.brand;$("contrast").textContent=T.contrast;$("print").textContent=T.print;
  rail();
  const locked=s.gate&&!gateOK.every(Boolean);
  const tryBody=s.prompt
    ? `<div class="prompt"><div class="ptxt">${s.prompt}</div>
       <footer><span>${T.promptHint}</span><button class="copy" id="copyBtn">${T.copy}</button></footer></div>`
    : `<div class="noai"><b>${T.noAiT}</b><ul>${s.noai.map(x=>`<li>${x}</li>`).join("")}</ul></div>`;

  $("station").innerHTML=`
  <div class="head">
    <div class="eyebrow">${T.station(idx+1)}</div><h1>${s.n}</h1>
    <div class="meta">
      <div><span>${T.mTime}</span><b>20 ${lang==="th"?"นาที":"min"}</b></div>
      <div><span>${T.mFormat}</span><b>${T.format}</b></div>
      <div><span>${T.mTrack}</span><b>${T.track}</b></div>
      <div><span>${T.mOut}</span><b>${s.out}</b></div>
    </div>
    ${s.gate?`<div class="gate"><h3>${T.gateH}</h3><p>${T.gateP}</p>
      ${T.gateItems.map((g,i)=>`<div class="gitem"><button class="check" data-g="${i}" aria-pressed="${gateOK[i]}">✓</button><p>${g}</p></div>`).join("")}</div>`:""}
  </div>

  <div class="veil ${locked?"locked":""}">
    <section class="step">
      <header><span class="badge">1</span><h2>${T.steps[0]}</h2><span class="mins">${s.watch.d}</span></header>
      <div class="video"><span class="play">▶</span><span><b>${s.watch.t}</b><span>${T.watchCap}</span></span></div>
      ${chk(0)}
    </section>
    <section class="step">
      <header><span class="badge">2</span><h2>${T.steps[1]}</h2></header>
      ${tryBody}
      <p class="expect"><b>${T.expectT}:</b> ${s.expect}</p>
      <div class="stuck"><b>${T.stuckT}</b><br>${s.stuck}</div>
      ${s.calc?`<div class="calc"><h3>${T.calcH}</h3><p class="sub">${T.calcP}</p>
        <div class="cfields">
          <div><label for="cb">${T.cBefore}</label><input id="cb" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="${calc.b}"></div>
          <div><label for="ca">${T.cAfter}</label><input id="ca" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="${calc.a}"></div>
          <div><label for="cf">${T.cFreq}</label><input id="cf" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="${calc.f}"></div>
        </div>${calcOut()}</div>`:""}
      ${chk(1)}
    </section>
    <section class="step">
      <header><span class="badge">3</span><h2>${T.steps[2]}</h2></header>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.02rem">${s.make.t}</p>
      <div class="stuck" style="border-color:var(--ok)"><b>${T.doneT}</b><br>${s.make.d}</div>
      ${chk(2)}
    </section>
    <section class="step">
      <header><span class="badge">4</span><h2>${T.steps[3]}</h2></header>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.02rem">${s.show.t}</p>
      ${chk(3)}
    </section>
    ${locked?`<div class="veilmsg">${T.gateLocked}</div>`:""}
  </div>

  <div class="foot">
    ${idx>0?`<button class="ghost" id="prev">${T.back}</button>`:""}
    <button class="primary" id="nxt">${idx<3?T.next:T.finish}</button>
    <p class="pausenote">${T.pause}</p>
  </div>`;

  const cp=$("copyBtn");
  if(cp)cp.onclick=()=>{navigator.clipboard&&navigator.clipboard.writeText(s.prompt);cp.textContent=T.copied;
    setTimeout(()=>{const b=$("copyBtn");if(b)b.textContent=T.copy},1600)};
  ["cb","ca","cf"].forEach((id,i)=>{const e=$(id);if(e)e.oninput=()=>{calc[["b","a","f"][i]]=e.value.replace(/[^0-9]/g,"");
    const k=document.activeElement.id;render();const n=$(k);if(n){n.focus();n.setSelectionRange(n.value.length,n.value.length)}}});
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-g]").forEach(c=>c.onclick=()=>{gateOK[+c.dataset.g]=!gateOK[+c.dataset.g];render()});
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-s]").forEach(c=>c.onclick=()=>{
    const i=+c.dataset.s,d=done[idx]||[];done[idx]=d.includes(i)?d.filter(x=>x!==i):[...d,i];render()});
  const p=$("prev");if(p)p.onclick=()=>{idx--;render();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:"smooth"})};
  $("nxt").onclick=()=>{if(idx<3){idx++;render();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:"smooth"})}};
}
document.querySelectorAll("[data-scale]").forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-scale]").forEach(x=>x.setAttribute("aria-pressed",x===b));
  document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--scale",b.dataset.scale)});
document.querySelectorAll("[data-lang]").forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-lang]").forEach(x=>x.setAttribute("aria-pressed",x===b));
  lang=b.dataset.lang;document.documentElement.lang=lang;render()});
$("contrast").onclick=e=>{const on=document.documentElement.dataset.contrast!=="high";
  document.documentElement.dataset.contrast=on?"high":"normal";e.target.setAttribute("aria-pressed",on)};
$("print").onclick=()=>window.print();
{
  const qp = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("lang");
  if (qp === "en") {
    lang = "en";
    document.documentElement.lang = "en";
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-lang]").forEach(b=>b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.lang==="en")));
  }
}
render();
</script>
</body>
</html>
